            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 22-year-old male patient admitted to our clinic with mild pain in left knee. Pain had started 10 years ago and there was no history of trauma. Pain was increased with kneeling. No abnormality was detected on physical examination. Imaging results revealed proximal tibiofibular synostosis in left knee.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
